IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 7), 1999 Revised Edition (1 July 1999), made under section 131 of the Telecommunication Authority of Singapore Act (Cap. 323), the "repealed Act" of the Telecommunications Act 1999.
-- Text: TA1999-DEAL99 under subjects/sg/telecommunications-dealers-regulations-1999/registers/source-bundle/ (the e-Gazette's copy, deposited 2026-11-04 from the follow-up list; sha256 in the .meta.json).
-- The title page prints "Rg 7, 1995 Ed., G.N. No. S 327/94, Amended by S 88/95, S 70/96, S 425/96, S 166/98, S 540/98, REVISED EDITION 1999 (1.7.1999)".  None of those instruments is deposited; the Revised Edition incorporates them.
--
-- WHEN IT APPLIES.  The Telecommunications Act 1999 came into operation on 1 December 1999 (s 3(1)); s 98(2) continues subsidiary legislation "made under the repealed Act ... and in force immediately before 1 December 1999 ... as if made under
-- this Act until it is revoked or repealed by subsidiary legislation made under this Act" (TA1999.txt:7097-7102; encoded as `s 98(2): ...` in sgta-part9-general.l4).  So this text answers from 1 December 1999.
-- It ended on 1 April 2003: reg 26 of the Telecommunications (Dealers) Regulations 2003, G.N. No. S 185/2003, reads "The Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7) are revoked.", and reg 1 puts those Regulations in operation on 2nd April 2003
-- (TA1999-RG6-S185-2003.txt; encoded in sgta-i-rg6-as-made.l4).  Until Part 3 of the follow-up (2026-11-04) this end day was an assumption.
-- Its one amendment held is S 362/2001, the Telecommunication (Dealers) (Amendment) Regulations 2001 (first published 30 July 2001, made under s 74 of the Act, in operation 1 August 2001 except reg 4(a), deemed from 21 January 2000), which replaces reg 15 and reg 32 and
-- amends the First Schedule (TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001.txt, encoded at the end of this module).  From 1 August 2001 the 1999 text is not the text: the version table (sgta-i-versions.l4) has the row.  Other amendments after 1 July 1999 are not known.
-- A date before 1 December 1999 answers NOTHING (the TAS Act period is outside the scope of the Telecommunications Act encoding).
--
-- WHAT IT DOES.  Part II licenses dealers (Dealer's Individual Licence, reg 4; Dealer's Class Licence, reg 4A, deemed for dealers in type-approved or Fifth Schedule equipment); Part III restricts import, manufacture and sale
-- (reg 20, 23, 24: sale of line-connected or radio-communication equipment needs approval of the type by the Authority, except Fifth Schedule equipment); the schedules list prohibited equipment (First: "1. Scanning Receivers" among 8 items), fees,
-- class licence conditions and the equipment not requiring approval (Fifth).  Reg 30 makes the dealer tell a purchaser of the need for a licence "if the purchaser or hirer is required under the Act or any regulations made thereunder to obtain any licence for the possession,
-- operation, installation or use of that equipment".  These Regulations regulate dealers.
-- Reg 24(1) is the approval the Order O 3 names ("approved for sale by the Authority under regulation 24 (1) of the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7)"), and the Fifth Schedule is the one O 3 names in its para 2(b).

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:116 | Citation
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:117 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:118 | (Dealers) Regulations.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 1 (citation) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:116-118)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 26 of S 185/2003, in operation 2 April 2003)` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 1 12 1999) AND d LESS THAN (Date 2 4 2003)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:120 | Definitions
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:121 | 2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:122 | ‘‘authorised officer’’ means any person authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:123 | Authority to act on its behalf;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:124 | ‘‘dealer’’ means a person who manufactures, imports, sells, hires,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:125 | offers or possesses for sale, hire or hire-purchase any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:126 | equipment which is capable of being used for the purpose of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:127 | telecommunication, and includes his employees;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:128 | ‘‘Dealer’s Class Licence’’ means a licence granted under
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:129 | regulation 4A;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:130 | ‘‘Dealer’s Individual Licence’’ means a licence granted under
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:131 | regulation 4;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:132 | ‘‘identity card’’ means an identity card issued under the National
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:133 | Registration Act (Cap. 201);
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:134 | ‘‘licence’’ means a Telecommunication Dealer’s Licence granted
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:135 | under these Regulations;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:136 | ‘‘licensee’’ means a person to whom a licence is granted under
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:137 | these Regulations, and includes his employees;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:138 | ‘‘sale’’ includes every transaction of or in the nature of barter or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:139 | exchange, every transaction of hire or hire-purchase and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:140 | every transaction by which any goods are pawned or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:141 | hypothecated or as the result of which the ownership of or an
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:142 | interest in goods is or may be transferred or created;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:143 | ‘‘Telecommunication Dealer’s Licence’’ means a Dealer’s Class
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:144 | Licence granted under regulation 4A or a Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:145 | Licence granted under regulation 4;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:150 | ‘‘telecommunication equipment’’ means any appliance, apparatus
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:151 | or accessory used or intended to be used for telecommuni-
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:152 | cation;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:153 | ‘‘type-approval labels’’ means labels stating or indicating that the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:154 | telecommunication equipment is type-approved equipment;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:155 | ‘‘type-approved equipment’’ means any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:156 | equipment approved for sale under regulation 24 (1).
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:159 | PART II
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:160 | LICENSING CONDITIONS
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 2 (definitions) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:120-160)
GIVEN `the person manufactures, imports, sells, hires, offers or possesses for sale, hire or hire-purchase equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is capable of being used for the purpose of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the person is a "dealer"` MEANS
    ((`the person manufactures, imports, sells, hires, offers or possesses for sale, hire or hire-purchase equipment` AND `the equipment is capable of being used for the purpose of telecommunication`)
      OR `the person is an employee of such a person`)

GIVEN `the equipment has been approved for sale under regulation 24(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the equipment is "type-approved equipment"` MEANS `the equipment has been approved for sale under regulation 24(1)`

GIVEN `the person holds a Dealer's Class Licence granted under regulation 4A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a Dealer's Individual Licence granted under regulation 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the person holds a "Telecommunication Dealer's Licence"` MEANS
    `the person holds a Dealer's Class Licence granted under regulation 4A` OR `the person holds a Dealer's Individual Licence granted under regulation 4`

GIVEN `the transaction is barter, exchange, hire, hire-purchase, pawning or hypothecation, or one by which ownership of or an interest in goods is or may be transferred or created` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the transaction is a "sale"` MEANS `the transaction is barter, exchange, hire, hire-purchase, pawning or hypothecation, or one by which ownership of or an interest in goods is or may be transferred or created`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:162 | Licensing authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:163 | 3. The licensing authority in respect of every licence granted under
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:164 | these Regulations shall be the Authority with the consent of, or under
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:165 | the terms of a general authority given by, the Minister.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 3 (licensing authority) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:162-165)
GIVEN `the Authority acts with the consent of, or under the terms of a general authority given by, the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 3: the Authority is the licensing authority for the licence` MEANS `the Authority acts with the consent of, or under the terms of a general authority given by, the Minister`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:167 | Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:168 | 4.—(1) No person, other than a holder of a Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:169 | Licence granted by the Authority, shall manufacture, import, hire,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:170 | sell, or offer or possess for sale, any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:171 | other than type-approved equipment or telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:172 | equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:173 | (2) The Authority shall, when granting a Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:174 | Licence, specify the types of telecommunication equipment which the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:175 | dealer may manufacture, import, hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:176 | (3) A holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence may sell telecom-
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:177 | munication equipment that is not type-approved equipment or not set
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:178 | out in the Fifth Schedule only —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:179 | (a) to another holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence; or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:180 | (b) to a person, other than a holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:181 | for re-export purposes and not for use in Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:182 | (4) A dealer shall obtain a Dealer’s Individual Licence for each of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:183 | the premises under his control or occupation at which he
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:184 | manufactures, imports, hires, sells, offers or possesses for sale any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:185 | telecommunication equipment.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4 (Dealer's Individual Licence) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:167-185)
GIVEN `the person manufactures, imports, hires, sells, or offers or possesses for sale the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a Dealer's Individual Licence granted by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is type-approved equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS
        `the person manufactures, imports, hires, sells, or offers or possesses for sale the equipment`
    AND (NOT `the person holds a Dealer's Individual Licence granted by the Authority`)
    AND (NOT (`the equipment is type-approved equipment` OR `the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule`))

GIVEN `the dealer deals in a type of equipment the Authority specified when granting the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(2): the dealer may manufacture, import, hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale the type of equipment` MEANS `the dealer deals in a type of equipment the Authority specified when granting the licence`

GIVEN `the sale is to another holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is to a person other than a holder of a Dealer's Class Licence, for re-export purposes and not for use in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(3): the holder may sell equipment that is not type-approved equipment or not set out in the Fifth Schedule` MEANS
    `the sale is to another holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence` OR `the sale is to a person other than a holder of a Dealer's Class Licence, for re-export purposes and not for use in Singapore`

GIVEN `the dealer holds a Dealer's Individual Licence for the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(4): the dealer has obtained the licence the regulation requires for the premises` MEANS `the dealer holds a Dealer's Individual Licence for the premises`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:189 | Dealer’s Class Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:190 | 4A.—(1) A dealer who manufactures, imports, hires, sells, or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:191 | offers or possesses for sale any type-approved equipment or tele-
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:192 | communication equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule shall be
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:193 | deemed to have been granted a Dealer’s Class Licence for that
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:194 | purpose.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:195 | (2) A dealer who is deemed to have been granted a Dealer’s Class
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:196 | Licence shall, in addition to any requirement imposed under these
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:197 | Regulations, comply with the conditions of licence set out in the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:198 | Fourth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:199 | (3) The Authority may suspend or cancel a Dealer’s Class Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:200 | by notice in writing addressed to the licensee on the ground that the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:201 | licensee had —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:202 | (a) in registering with the Authority, furnished false, misleading
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:203 | or inaccurate information;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:204 | (b) misused any telecommunication equipment; or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:205 | (c) failed to comply with any of the provisions of the Act or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:206 | these Regulations or any condition of licence set out in the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:207 | Fourth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:208 | (4) Where a Dealer’s Class Licence is suspended or cancelled by
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:209 | the Authority, no compensation shall be paid by the Authority to the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:210 | licensee and no fee or part thereof shall be refunded by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:211 | to the licensee in respect of the unexpired period of such licence.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4A (Dealer's Class Licence) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:189-211)
GIVEN `the dealer manufactures, imports, hires, sells, or offers or possesses for sale type-approved equipment or equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4A(1): the dealer is deemed to have been granted a Dealer's Class Licence for that purpose` MEANS `the dealer manufactures, imports, hires, sells, or offers or possesses for sale type-approved equipment or equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule`

GIVEN `the dealer complies with the conditions of licence in the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4A(2): the dealer is meeting the requirement` MEANS `the dealer complies with the conditions of licence in the Fourth Schedule`

GIVEN `in registering with the Authority the licensee furnished false, misleading or inaccurate information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee misused telecommunication equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee failed to comply with a provision of the Act or the Regulations or a condition in the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4A(3): the Authority may suspend or cancel the Dealer's Class Licence by notice in writing` MEANS
    `in registering with the Authority the licensee furnished false, misleading or inaccurate information` OR `the licensee misused telecommunication equipment` OR `the licensee failed to comply with a provision of the Act or the Regulations or a condition in the Fourth Schedule`

GIVEN `the Dealer's Class Licence is suspended or cancelled by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4A(4): no compensation is paid and no fee is refunded for the unexpired period` MEANS `the Dealer's Class Licence is suspended or cancelled by the Authority`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:213 | Use for demonstration
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:214 | 5.—(1) Notwithstanding regulation 4 (1), a person may, subject to
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:215 | the Authority’s prior approval, operate any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:216 | equipment for demonstration purposes only without a Telecommu-
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:217 | nication Dealer’s Licence.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:218 | (2) No dealer licensed under these Regulations shall, except with
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:219 | the Authority’s prior approval, operate any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:220 | equipment for demonstration purposes.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 5 (use for demonstration) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:213-220)
GIVEN `the Authority gave its prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the operation is for demonstration purposes only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 5(1): the person may operate the equipment without a Telecommunication Dealer's Licence` MEANS
    `the Authority gave its prior approval` AND `the operation is for demonstration purposes only`

GIVEN `the dealer operates equipment for demonstration purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gave its prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 5(2): the dealer contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the dealer operates equipment for demonstration purposes` AND (NOT `the Authority gave its prior approval`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:222 | Application for Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:223 | 6.—(1) Every application for a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:224 | be made in such form and manner which the Authority may, from
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:229 | time to time, determine and shall be supported by such information
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:230 | as the Authority may require.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:231 | (2) A licensee shall notify the Authority of any change in his
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:232 | personal particulars specified in a Dealer’s Individual Licence within
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:233 | 14 days of such change.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:234 | (3) A Dealer’s Individual Licence granted under these
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:235 | Regulations shall be valid for such period as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:236 | determine unless revoked or suspended in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:237 | provisions of the Act or these Regulations, and shall be subject to
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:238 | such conditions, restrictions and limitations as the Authority may,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:239 | from time to time, determine.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:240 | (4) The Authority may at any time vary all or any of the conditions
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:241 | upon which a Dealer’s Individual Licence is granted or impose
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:242 | additional conditions.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:243 | (5) A licensee shall, at his own expense, comply with the varied or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:244 | additional conditions referred to in paragraph (4).
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 6 (application for Dealer's Individual Licence) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:222-244)
GIVEN `the application is in the form and manner the Authority determines and supported by the information it requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 6(1): the application is in order` MEANS `the application is in the form and manner the Authority determines and supported by the information it requires`

GIVEN `days after the change in personal particulars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 6(2): the licensee has notified the Authority within the time` MEANS `days after the change in personal particulars` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `the licence has been revoked or suspended in accordance with the Act or the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 6(3): the licence remains valid for the period the Authority determined` MEANS NOT `the licence has been revoked or suspended in accordance with the Act or the Regulations`

GIVEN `the Authority has varied the conditions or imposed additional conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee complies with them at its own expense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 6(4) and (5): the licensee is meeting the varied or additional conditions` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority has varied the conditions or imposed additional conditions`) OR `the licensee complies with them at its own expense`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:246 | No assignment, transfer, etc., of benefits of Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:247 | Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:248 | 7. Except with the consent in writing of the Authority, a licensee
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:249 | shall not assign, transfer, sublet or otherwise dispose of the benefit of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:250 | any Dealer’s Individual Licence granted under these Regulations, or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:251 | permit another person to participate in any of the benefits, powers or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:252 | authority granted under such licence.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 7 (no assignment, transfer, etc.) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:246-252)
GIVEN `the licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or otherwise disposes of the benefit of the licence, or permits another person to participate in its benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 7: the licensee contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or otherwise disposes of the benefit of the licence, or permits another person to participate in its benefits` AND (NOT `the Authority consented in writing`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:254 | Employees of licensee
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:255 | 8. The licensee shall ensure that his employees comply with the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:256 | provisions of the Act, these Regulations and the conditions of the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:257 | licence.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 8 (employees of licensee) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:254-257)
GIVEN `the licensee ensures that its employees comply with the Act, the Regulations and the conditions of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 8: the licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS `the licensee ensures that its employees comply with the Act, the Regulations and the conditions of the licence`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:259 | Restriction on grant of licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:260 | 9. No person shall be granted a Dealer’s Individual Licence and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:261 | no person shall be deemed to have been granted a Dealer’s Class
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:262 | Licence except —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:263 | (a) a person who is a citizen of Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:264 | (b) a company incorporated under the Companies Act
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:265 | (Cap. 50);
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:269 | (c) a business registered under the Business Registration Act
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:270 | (Cap. 32); or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:271 | (d) such other person as the Authority may, in its discretion,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:272 | think fit.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 9 (restriction on grant of licence) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:259-272)
GIVEN `the person is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company incorporated under the Companies Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a business registered under the Business Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority in its discretion thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 9: the person may be granted a Dealer's Individual Licence or be deemed granted a Dealer's Class Licence` MEANS
    `the person is a citizen of Singapore` OR `the person is a company incorporated under the Companies Act` OR `the person is a business registered under the Business Registration Act` OR `the Authority in its discretion thinks fit`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:274 | Replacement of Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:275 | 10. If the Authority is satisfied that any Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:276 | Licence issued by it has been lost, destroyed or defaced, the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:277 | Authority may, upon payment of a fee of $5, issue a replacement
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:278 | licence.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 10 (replacement of Dealer's Individual Licence) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:274-278)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that the licence has been lost, destroyed or defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee of $5 has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 10: the Authority may issue a replacement licence` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied that the licence has been lost, destroyed or defaced` AND `the fee of $5 has been paid`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:280 | Renewal of Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:281 | 11. Every application for the renewal of a Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:282 | Licence under these Regulations shall be in such form and manner as
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:283 | the Authority may require.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 11 (renewal) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:280-283)
GIVEN `the application for renewal is in the form and manner the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 11: the application for renewal is in order` MEANS `the application for renewal is in the form and manner the Authority requires`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:285 | Suspension and revocation of Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:286 | 12.—(1) The Authority may suspend or revoke a Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:287 | Individual Licence granted under these Regulations by notice in
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:288 | writing addressed to the licensee on the ground that —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:289 | (a) the licensee had in his application for the Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:290 | Individual Licence furnished false, misleading or inaccurate
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:291 | information; or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:292 | (b) there has been misuse of any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:293 | or failure to comply with any of the provisions of the Act or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:294 | these Regulations or with any condition of the Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:295 | Individual Licence.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:296 | (2) The licensee whose Dealer’s Individual Licence is suspended
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:297 | or revoked shall, if required by the Authority, surrender the Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:298 | Individual Licence to the Authority within such time as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:299 | may specify.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:300 | (3) Where a Dealer’s Individual Licence is suspended or revoked
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:301 | by the Authority or where a Dealer’s Individual Licence is terminated
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:302 | by a licensee, no compensation shall be paid by the Authority to the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:303 | licensee and no fee or part thereof shall be refunded by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:304 | to the licensee in respect of the unexpired period of such licence.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 12 (suspension and revocation) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:285-304)
GIVEN `the licensee furnished false, misleading or inaccurate information in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been misuse of telecommunication equipment or a failure to comply with a provision of the Act or the Regulations or a condition of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 12(1): the Authority may suspend or revoke the Dealer's Individual Licence by notice in writing` MEANS
    `the licensee furnished false, misleading or inaccurate information in the application` OR `there has been misuse of telecommunication equipment or a failure to comply with a provision of the Act or the Regulations or a condition of the licence`

GIVEN `the Authority requires surrender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee surrenders the licence within the time the Authority specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 12(2): the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority requires surrender`) OR `the licensee surrenders the licence within the time the Authority specifies`

GIVEN `the licence is suspended or revoked by the Authority, or terminated by the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 12(3): no compensation is paid and no fee is refunded for the unexpired period` MEANS `the licence is suspended or revoked by the Authority, or terminated by the licensee`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:311 | Fees
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:312 | 13.—(1) The fee payable for —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:313 | (a) a Dealer’s Individual Licence granted under regulation 4
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:314 | shall be $400 per annum; and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:315 | (b) a Dealer’s Class Licence granted under regulation 4A shall
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:316 | be $50 for every 5 years.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:317 | (2) Paragraph (1) (b) shall not apply to a holder of both a Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:318 | Individual Licence and a Dealer’s Class Licence.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:319 | (3) All fees shall be paid in advance and if any fee remains unpaid
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:320 | 7 days after the date on which a licence should have been renewed,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:321 | the following late payment fee shall be charged:
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:322 | (a) where the licence is renewed after 7 days but less than 15
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:323 | days following the expiration of the previous licence, $10;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:324 | (b) where the licence is renewed after 14 days but less than 31
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:325 | days following the expiration of the previous licence, $20;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:326 | and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:327 | (c) where the licence is renewed after 30 days following the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:328 | expiration of the previous licence, $50.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13 (fees) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:311-328)
GIVEN kind IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(1): the fee payable in dollars for the licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF kind EQUALS "Dealer's Individual Licence, per annum" THEN JUST 400
           IF kind EQUALS "Dealer's Class Licence, for every 5 years" THEN JUST 50
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the person holds both a Dealer's Individual Licence and a Dealer's Class Licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(2): paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` MEANS `the person holds both a Dealer's Individual Licence and a Dealer's Class Licence`

GIVEN `days after the expiration of the previous licence on which the licence is renewed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(3): the late payment fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `days after the expiration of the previous licence on which the licence is renewed` AT MOST 7 THEN 0
           IF `days after the expiration of the previous licence on which the licence is renewed` LESS THAN 15 THEN 10
           IF `days after the expiration of the previous licence on which the licence is renewed` LESS THAN 31 THEN 20
           OTHERWISE 50

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:330 | Equipment to be used for lawful purpose, safe manner, etc.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:331 | 14. A dealer shall ensure that any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:332 | in his possession is not used for any unlawful purpose and is worked
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:333 | by him in a manner which is safe and which does not impair or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:334 | interfere with the efficient and convenient working or maintenance of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:335 | any other telecommunication system or service authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:336 | Authority.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 14 (equipment to be used for lawful purpose, safe manner, etc.) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:330-336)
GIVEN `the dealer ensures the equipment in his possession is not used for any unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer works it in a manner which is safe and does not impair or interfere with the efficient and convenient working or maintenance of any other authorised telecommunication system or service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 14: the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the dealer ensures the equipment in his possession is not used for any unlawful purpose` AND `the dealer works it in a manner which is safe and does not impair or interfere with the efficient and convenient working or maintenance of any other authorised telecommunication system or service`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:338 | Examination of Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:339 | 15. A police officer not below the rank of sergeant or an
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:340 | authorised officer shall be entitled, upon production of proof of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:341 | identity, to inspect any Dealer’s Individual Licence granted under
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:342 | these Regulations or, if it is not immediately available, require its
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:343 | production at the office of the Authority or a named police station
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:344 | within a reasonable period.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 15 (examination of licence) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:338-344)
GIVEN `the person is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer produced proof of identity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 15: the officer is entitled to inspect the Dealer's Individual Licence` MEANS
    `the person is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an authorised officer` AND `the officer produced proof of identity`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:348 | Inspection of equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:349 | 16.—(1) The Authority may appoint authorised officers as
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:350 | inspection officers for the inspection and examination of any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:351 | equipment licensed under these Regulations, any premises owned or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:352 | occupied by a dealer and any telecommunication equipment found
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:353 | therein.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:354 | (2) For the purpose of ensuring that the Act, these Regulations
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:355 | and any condition of a licence granted hereunder are complied with,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:356 | inspection officers shall be entitled, at any time and upon production
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:357 | of proof of identity, to enter any land, building, vessel, aircraft or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:358 | vehicle where any telecommunication equipment is kept or stored
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:359 | and inspect, examine or test such equipment.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 16 (inspection of equipment) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:348-359)
GIVEN `the Authority appointed the officer as an inspection officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer produced proof of identity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to ensure that the Act, the Regulations and the conditions of a licence are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 16(2): the inspection officer is entitled at any time to enter the land, building, vessel, aircraft or vehicle and inspect, examine or test the equipment` MEANS
    `the Authority appointed the officer as an inspection officer` AND `the officer produced proof of identity` AND `the purpose is to ensure that the Act, the Regulations and the conditions of a licence are complied with`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:361 | Duty to give access
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:362 | 17. No person shall —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:363 | (a) refuse entry to an authorised officer to any land, building,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:364 | vessel, aircraft or vehicle to inspect, examine or test any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:365 | telecommunication equipment contained or stored therein;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:366 | or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:367 | (b) in any way obstruct or hinder an authorised officer in the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:368 | execution of a duty imposed or power conferred upon that
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:369 | officer by the Act, these Regulations or by any other written
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:370 | law.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 17 (duty to give access) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:361-370)
GIVEN `the person refuses entry to an authorised officer to inspect, examine or test telecommunication equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obstructs or hinders an authorised officer in the execution of a duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 17: the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the person refuses entry to an authorised officer to inspect, examine or test telecommunication equipment` OR `the person obstructs or hinders an authorised officer in the execution of a duty or power`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:372 | Secrecy
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:373 | 18.—(1) Except as otherwise provided in these Regulations or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:374 | by the terms and conditions of a licence granted under these
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:375 | Regulations, every dealer having access to any telecommunication —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:376 | (a) shall hold strictly secret all such telecommunication, other
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:377 | than those transmitted or sent for general information,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:378 | which may pass through his hands or come to his knowledge;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:379 | and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:380 | (b) shall not, directly or indirectly, disclose the contents thereof
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:381 | except to a person entitled to become acquainted with the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:382 | telecommunication or to an authorised officer or to a court
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:383 | and shall not make any other use of such telecommunication.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:391 | (2) No dealer having unauthorised access to telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:392 | shall print or publish or cause to be printed or published in any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:393 | newspaper, pamphlet, book or document, any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:394 | that may pass through his hands or come to his knowledge, whether
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:395 | such telecommunication be for private or general reception.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 18 (secrecy) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:372-395)
GIVEN `the dealer has access to a telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the telecommunication was transmitted or sent for general information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer holds it strictly secret` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer discloses its contents to a person other than a person entitled to become acquainted with it, an authorised officer or a court, or makes any other use of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 18(1): the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    (NOT `the dealer has access to a telecommunication`) OR `the telecommunication was transmitted or sent for general information` OR (`the dealer holds it strictly secret` AND (NOT `the dealer discloses its contents to a person other than a person entitled to become acquainted with it, an authorised officer or a court, or makes any other use of it`))

GIVEN `the dealer has unauthorised access to a telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer prints or publishes it or causes it to be printed or published in a newspaper, pamphlet, book or document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 18(2): the dealer contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the dealer has unauthorised access to a telecommunication` AND `the dealer prints or publishes it or causes it to be printed or published in a newspaper, pamphlet, book or document`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:397 | Restrictions on transmission
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:398 | 19.—(1) No dealer shall transmit or permit the transmission of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:399 | superfluous signals.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:400 | (2) No test, trial or practical transmission shall be permitted except
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:401 | in such circumstances as to preclude the possibility of interference
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:402 | with any other telecommunication.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:403 | (3) All tests, unless prior approval from the Authority has been
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:404 | obtained, shall be conducted on dummy load.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:405 | (4) No dealer shall transmit or permit the transmission of —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:406 | (a) any message containing indecent, obscene or offensive
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:407 | language;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:408 | (b) any message for an improper or illegal purpose;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:409 | (c) any message which interferes with the operation of any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:410 | authorised telecommunication equipment; or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:411 | (d) any message which to his knowledge is false or misleading
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:412 | and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:413 | endanger the safety of any person or of a place or premises,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:414 | vessel, aircraft or vehicle.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:417 | PART III
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:418 | IMPORT, MANUFACTURE AND SALE OF
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:419 | TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 19 (restrictions on transmission) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:397-419)
GIVEN `the dealer transmits or permits the transmission of superfluous signals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the test, trial or practical transmission is in circumstances that preclude the possibility of interference with any other telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the test is conducted on dummy load, or the Authority's prior approval has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer transmits or permits the transmission of a message containing indecent, obscene or offensive language, or sent for an improper or illegal purpose, or interfering with the operation of any authorised telecommunication equipment, or known to be false or misleading and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or endanger safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 19: the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS
        (NOT `the dealer transmits or permits the transmission of superfluous signals`)
    AND `the test, trial or practical transmission is in circumstances that preclude the possibility of interference with any other telecommunication`
    AND `the test is conducted on dummy load, or the Authority's prior approval has been obtained`
    AND (NOT `the dealer transmits or permits the transmission of a message containing indecent, obscene or offensive language, or sent for an improper or illegal purpose, or interfering with the operation of any authorised telecommunication equipment, or known to be false or misleading and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or endanger safety`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:421 | Restrictions on importation of telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:422 | 20.—(1) Notwithstanding the grant of a Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:423 | Dealer’s Licence, no person shall import any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:424 | equipment without the prior approval of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:425 | (2) No approval shall be granted by the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:426 | paragraph (1) for the import of any telecommunication equipment set
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:430 | out in the First Schedule except where approved by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:431 | upon such terms and conditions as may be imposed.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:432 | (3) A person applying for approval under paragraph (1) shall
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:433 | furnish such particulars as may be required by the Authority and shall
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:434 | have his permit issued under the Regulation of Imports and Exports
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:435 | Regulations (Cap. 272A, Rg 1) for the equipment endorsed by the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:436 | Authority before such equipment is brought into Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:437 | (4) No person shall —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:438 | (a) furnish false or misleading information to the Authority for
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:439 | the purpose of obtaining the approval of the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:440 | under paragraph (1); or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:441 | (b) falsify or fabricate any decision that the Authority may make
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:442 | upon the application for approval under paragraph (1).
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:443 | (5) Where any person furnishes any false or misleading
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:444 | information to the Authority for the purpose of obtaining the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:445 | approval of the Authority or falsifies or fabricates any decision that
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:446 | the Authority may make upon the application for approval, the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:447 | approval shall be null and void.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20 (restrictions on importation) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:421-447)
GIVEN `the person imports the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gave its prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(1): the person contravenes the regulation, despite the grant of a Telecommunication Dealer's Licence` MEANS
    `the person imports the equipment` AND (NOT `the Authority gave its prior approval`)

GIVEN `the equipment is set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approves upon terms and conditions it imposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(2): approval may be granted for the import of the equipment` MEANS
    (NOT `the equipment is set out in the First Schedule`) OR `the Authority approves upon terms and conditions it imposes`

GIVEN `the applicant furnished the particulars the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant had the permit under the Regulation of Imports and Exports Regulations endorsed by the Authority before the equipment is brought into Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(3): the applicant has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the applicant furnished the particulars the Authority requires` AND `the applicant had the permit under the Regulation of Imports and Exports Regulations endorsed by the Authority before the equipment is brought into Singapore`

GIVEN `the person furnishes false or misleading information to obtain approval under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person falsifies or fabricates a decision of the Authority on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(4): the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the person furnishes false or misleading information to obtain approval under paragraph (1)` OR `the person falsifies or fabricates a decision of the Authority on the application`

GIVEN `the approval was obtained by furnishing false or misleading information or by falsifying or fabricating a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(5): the approval is null and void` MEANS `the approval was obtained by furnishing false or misleading information or by falsifying or fabricating a decision`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:449 | Power of Authority to order production of equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:450 | 21. The Authority may direct that any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:451 | equipment that is imported be produced by the dealer for testing or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:452 | inspection by the Authority and all expenses incurred in connection
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:453 | therewith shall be borne by the dealer.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 21 (power to order production of equipment) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:449-453)
GIVEN `the equipment is imported` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority directs that it be produced by the dealer for testing or inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 21: the dealer must produce the equipment and bear all expenses connected with the testing or inspection` MEANS
    `the equipment is imported` AND `the Authority directs that it be produced by the dealer for testing or inspection`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:455 | Equipment imported for re-export
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:456 | 22. Any dealer who imports any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:457 | into Singapore for the purpose of re-export shall —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:458 | (a) unless the Authority otherwise directs, immediately move
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:459 | the telecommunication equipment into a free trade zone
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:460 | under the Free Trade Zones Act (Cap. 114) and keep it
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:461 | there pending re-export; and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:462 | (b) re-export the telecommunication equipment and furnish
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:463 | satisfactory evidence of the re-export to the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:464 | within such period of time as may be stipulated by the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:465 | Authority.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 22 (equipment imported for re-export) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:455-465)
GIVEN `the dealer imports the equipment for the purpose of re-export` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer immediately moves it into a free trade zone and keeps it there pending re-export, unless the Authority otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer re-exports it and furnishes satisfactory evidence to the Authority within the period stipulated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 22: the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    (NOT `the dealer imports the equipment for the purpose of re-export`) OR (`the dealer immediately moves it into a free trade zone and keeps it there pending re-export, unless the Authority otherwise directs` AND `the dealer re-exports it and furnishes satisfactory evidence to the Authority within the period stipulated`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:470 | Equipment declared for export
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:471 | 22A. Any dealer who imports any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:472 | into Singapore declaring it to be for export shall not, except with the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:473 | approval of the Authority, sell it to any person for use in Singapore.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 22A (equipment declared for export) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:470-473)
GIVEN `the dealer imports the equipment declaring it to be for export` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer sells it to a person for use in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 22A: the dealer contravenes the regulation` MEANS
    `the dealer imports the equipment declaring it to be for export` AND `the dealer sells it to a person for use in Singapore` AND (NOT `the Authority approved the sale`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:475 | Restrictions on manufacture and sale of telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:476 | equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:477 | 23. Notwithstanding the grant of any Telecommunication Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:478 | Licence, no person shall manufacture, sell or possess for sale —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:479 | (a) any telecommunication equipment set out in the First
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:480 | Schedule except where approved by the Authority upon
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:481 | such terms and conditions as may be imposed; or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:482 | (b) any telecommunication equipment which does not meet the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:483 | standards or specifications published by the Authority from
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:484 | time to time.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 23 (restrictions on manufacture and sale) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:475-484)
GIVEN `the person manufactures, sells or possesses for sale the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved it upon terms and conditions it imposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment does not meet the standards or specifications published by the Authority from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 23: the person contravenes the regulation, despite the grant of a Telecommunication Dealer's Licence` MEANS
    `the person manufactures, sells or possesses for sale the equipment`
    AND ((`the equipment is set out in the First Schedule` AND (NOT `the Authority approved it upon terms and conditions it imposes`)) OR `the equipment does not meet the standards or specifications published by the Authority from time to time`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:486 | Application for approval for sale
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:487 | 24.—(1) Subject to paragraph (2), no dealer shall sell —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:488 | (a) any type of telecommunication equipment to be used for
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:489 | connection to any telecommunication system or equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:490 | belonging to a telecommunication system licensee; or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:491 | (b) any type of radio-communication equipment to be used in
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:492 | Singapore,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:493 | unless the type of equipment has been approved by the Authority to
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:494 | be sold.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:495 | (2) No approval for sale under paragraph (1) is required in respect
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:496 | of the telecommunication equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:497 | (3) An application for approval to sell any equipment referred to
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:498 | in paragraph (1) is to be made to the Authority in such manner as the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:499 | Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:500 | (4) No person shall furnish false or misleading information
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:501 | to the Authority for the purpose of obtaining any approval under
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:502 | paragraph (1).
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:503 | (5) The fees for an application for approval to sell any equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:504 | referred to in paragraph (1) are set out in the Second Schedule.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24 (application for approval for sale) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:486-504)
GIVEN `the dealer sells a type of telecommunication equipment to be used for connection to a telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a telecommunication system licensee, or a type of radio-communication equipment to be used in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the type of equipment has been approved by the Authority to be sold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24(1) and (2): the dealer contravenes the regulation` MEANS
        `the dealer sells a type of telecommunication equipment to be used for connection to a telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a telecommunication system licensee, or a type of radio-communication equipment to be used in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the type of equipment has been approved by the Authority to be sold`)
    AND (NOT `the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule`)

GIVEN `the application is made in the manner the Authority determines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24(3): the application for approval to sell is in order` MEANS `the application is made in the manner the Authority determines`

GIVEN `the person furnishes false or misleading information to the Authority to obtain an approval under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24(4): the person contravenes the regulation` MEANS `the person furnishes false or misleading information to the Authority to obtain an approval under paragraph (1)`

GIVEN `the fee is the one set out in the Second Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24(5): the fee for the application is the one the Second Schedule sets out` MEANS `the fee is the one set out in the Second Schedule`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:508 | Sale of equipment in Fifth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:509 | 24A. A dealer who wishes to sell any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:510 | equipment set out in the Fifth Schedule shall —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:511 | (a) before selling the telecommunication equipment, ensure
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:512 | that the telecommunication equipment meets the standards
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:513 | and specifications as the Authority may publish from time to
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:514 | time for the sale of such telecommunication equipment;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:515 | (b) ensure that the telecommunication equipment interworks
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:516 | correctly with the relevant telecommunication system or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:517 | equipment belonging to the telecommunication system
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:518 | licensee to which it is connected; and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:519 | (c) cease to sell the telecommunication equipment if so directed
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:520 | by the Authority and dispose of the telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:521 | equipment at his expense in the manner directed by the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:522 | Authority.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24A (sale of equipment in Fifth Schedule) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:508-522)
GIVEN `before selling it the dealer ensures the equipment meets the standards and specifications the Authority publishes for the sale of such equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer ensures the equipment interworks correctly with the relevant telecommunication system or equipment of the licensee to which it is connected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority directs the dealer to cease to sell it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer ceases to sell it and disposes of it at his expense in the manner the Authority directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24A: the dealer who wishes to sell equipment in the Fifth Schedule is meeting the regulation` MEANS
        `before selling it the dealer ensures the equipment meets the standards and specifications the Authority publishes for the sale of such equipment`
    AND `the dealer ensures the equipment interworks correctly with the relevant telecommunication system or equipment of the licensee to which it is connected`
    AND ((NOT `the Authority directs the dealer to cease to sell it`) OR `the dealer ceases to sell it and disposes of it at his expense in the manner the Authority directs`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:524 | Particulars of equipment to be sold
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:525 | 25. A dealer shall furnish the Authority with such detailed specifi-
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:526 | cations and information on the types of telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:527 | equipment manufactured, sold or to be manufactured or sold by him
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:528 | as the Authority may, from time to time, specify.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 25 (particulars of equipment to be sold) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:524-528)
GIVEN `the dealer furnishes the Authority with the detailed specifications and information the Authority specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 25: the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS `the dealer furnishes the Authority with the detailed specifications and information the Authority specifies`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:530 | Licensee to give written undertaking
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:531 | 26. Where a dealer intends to manufacture or import any tele-
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:532 | communication equipment for export only, the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:533 | require the dealer to give a written undertaking that the equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:534 | will not be sold, offered or possessed for sale in Singapore.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 26 (licensee to give written undertaking) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:530-534)
GIVEN `the dealer intends to manufacture or import the equipment for export only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority requires a written undertaking that it will not be sold, offered or possessed for sale in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 26: the dealer must give the written undertaking` MEANS
    `the dealer intends to manufacture or import the equipment for export only` AND `the Authority requires a written undertaking that it will not be sold, offered or possessed for sale in Singapore`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:536 | Power to order disposal of equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:537 | 27. Where any person —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:538 | (a) imports any telecommunication equipment without the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:539 | approval of the Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:540 | (b) manufactures, sells, offers or possesses for sale any tele-
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:541 | communication equipment which does not meet the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:542 | standards or specifications published by the Authority from
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:543 | time to time,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:548 | the Authority may direct that person to dispose of the equipment in
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:549 | any manner which the Authority, in its discretion, thinks fit at the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:550 | licensee’s expense.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 27 (power to order disposal of equipment) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:536-550)
GIVEN `the person imports equipment without the Authority's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person manufactures, sells, offers or possesses for sale equipment that does not meet the standards or specifications published by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 27: the Authority may direct the person to dispose of the equipment in the manner it thinks fit, at the licensee's expense` MEANS
    `the person imports equipment without the Authority's approval` OR `the person manufactures, sells, offers or possesses for sale equipment that does not meet the standards or specifications published by the Authority`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:552 | Display of licence, approval labels, etc.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:553 | 28.—(1) A dealer shall —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:554 | (a) exhibit his Telecommunication Dealer’s Licence at all times
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:555 | in a prominent position at each place of his business;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:556 | (b) affix or ensure that there is affixed on all type-approved
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:557 | equipment intended for use in Singapore such type-approval
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:558 | labels provided by the Authority before such equipment is
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:559 | put on display or offered for sale;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:560 | (c) affix or ensure that there is affixed on any telecommuni-
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:561 | cation equipment sold in Singapore such other labels as the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:562 | Authority considers necessary before such equipment is put
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:563 | on display or offered for sale; and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:564 | (d) ensure that every advertisement, pamphlet or brochure
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:565 | relating to any telecommunication equipment which he sells
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:566 | or offers for sale contains such information as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:567 | may specify.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:568 | (2) A dealer shall display equipment which has been type-
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:569 | approved by the Authority separately from equipment the type of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:570 | which has not been approved at each place of his business.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:571 | (3) Where any telecommunication equipment the type of which
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:572 | has not been approved by the Authority under regulation 24 is sold
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:573 | or displayed, the dealer shall, at all times and in prominent positions
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:574 | at the premises where the equipment is sold or displayed, exhibit such
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:575 | signs or notices as the Authority may require.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:576 | (4) The dealer shall not affix any type-approval label provided by
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:577 | the Authority on any telecommunication equipment the type of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:578 | which has not been approved by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:579 | (5) A dealer shall comply with such rules of labelling as the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:580 | Authority may publish from time to time.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 28 (display of licence, approval labels, etc.) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:552-580)
GIVEN `the dealer exhibits his licence at all times in a prominent position at each place of his business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer affixes the type-approval labels provided by the Authority on all type-approved equipment intended for use in Singapore before it is put on display or offered for sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer affixes the other labels the Authority considers necessary on equipment sold in Singapore before it is put on display or offered for sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer ensures that every advertisement, pamphlet or brochure contains the information the Authority specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 28(1): the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the dealer exhibits his licence at all times in a prominent position at each place of his business`
    AND `the dealer affixes the type-approval labels provided by the Authority on all type-approved equipment intended for use in Singapore before it is put on display or offered for sale`
    AND `the dealer affixes the other labels the Authority considers necessary on equipment sold in Singapore before it is put on display or offered for sale`
    AND `the dealer ensures that every advertisement, pamphlet or brochure contains the information the Authority specifies`

GIVEN `the dealer displays type-approved equipment separately from equipment the type of which has not been approved at each place of his business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 28(2): the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS `the dealer displays type-approved equipment separately from equipment the type of which has not been approved at each place of his business`

GIVEN `equipment the type of which has not been approved under regulation 24 is sold or displayed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer exhibits at all times in prominent positions the signs or notices the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 28(3): the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    (NOT `equipment the type of which has not been approved under regulation 24 is sold or displayed`) OR `the dealer exhibits at all times in prominent positions the signs or notices the Authority requires`

GIVEN `the dealer affixes a type-approval label on equipment the type of which has not been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 28(4): the dealer contravenes the regulation` MEANS `the dealer affixes a type-approval label on equipment the type of which has not been approved`

GIVEN `the dealer complies with the rules of labelling the Authority publishes from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 28(5): the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS `the dealer complies with the rules of labelling the Authority publishes from time to time`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:582 | Records
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:583 | 29.—(1) A dealer shall maintain a record of every sale of any type
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:584 | of telecommunication equipment which the Authority may, from
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:588 | time to time, specify.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:589 | (2) The record shall contain such information, be kept in such form
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:590 | and be submitted to the Authority at such intervals as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:591 | may, from time to time, determine.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:592 | (3) Every purchaser or hirer of telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:593 | shall furnish to the dealer upon request, his name, identity card
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:594 | number and address.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:595 | (4) The dealer shall submit the particulars recorded under
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:596 | paragraph (1) at such intervals and in such format as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:597 | may specify.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:598 | (5) The dealer shall, at all reasonable times, permit an authorised
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:599 | officer to inspect and make copies of any entry in the record kept
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:600 | under paragraph (1).
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 29 (records) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:582-600)
GIVEN `the dealer maintains a record of every sale of the types of equipment the Authority specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record contains the information, is kept in the form and is submitted at the intervals the Authority determines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer submits the particulars at the intervals and in the format the Authority specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer permits an authorised officer at all reasonable times to inspect and make copies of any entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 29(1), (2), (4) and (5): the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the dealer maintains a record of every sale of the types of equipment the Authority specifies`
    AND `the record contains the information, is kept in the form and is submitted at the intervals the Authority determines`
    AND `the dealer submits the particulars at the intervals and in the format the Authority specifies`
    AND `the dealer permits an authorised officer at all reasonable times to inspect and make copies of any entry`

GIVEN `the purchaser or hirer furnishes to the dealer upon request his name, identity card number and address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 29(3): the purchaser or hirer is meeting the regulation` MEANS `the purchaser or hirer furnishes to the dealer upon request his name, identity card number and address`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:602 | Duty to inform purchasers and hirers of licensing requirements
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:603 | 30. The dealer shall inform every purchaser or hirer to whom he
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:604 | sells or lets any telecommunication equipment of the need to obtain
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:605 | a licence from the Authority if the purchaser or hirer is required
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:606 | under the Act or any regulations made thereunder to obtain any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:607 | licence for the possession, operation, installation or use of that
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:608 | equipment.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:610 | PART IV
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:611 | TESTING FEE
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 30 (duty to inform purchasers and hirers of licensing requirements) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:602-611)
GIVEN `the purchaser or hirer is required under the Act or any regulations made under it to obtain a licence for the possession, operation, installation or use of the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer informs the purchaser or hirer of the need to obtain a licence from the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 30: the dealer is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    (NOT `the purchaser or hirer is required under the Act or any regulations made under it to obtain a licence for the possession, operation, installation or use of the equipment`) OR `the dealer informs the purchaser or hirer of the need to obtain a licence from the Authority`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:613 | Fee for testing telecommunication equipment for personal use
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:614 | 31.—(1) The Authority may, at the request of any person
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:615 | intending to use any telecommunication equipment or type of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:616 | telecommunication equipment for personal use, test that equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:617 | to verify that the equipment is designed, constructed, installed,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:618 | established, maintained or operated in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:619 | Authority’s technical specifications and may, in its discretion, impose
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:620 | the fees specified in the Third Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:621 | (2) Paragraph (1) shall not apply to any radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:622 | equipment that is not type-approved equipment.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:627 | PART V
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:628 | MISCELLANEOUS
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 31 (fee for testing equipment for personal use) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:613-628)
GIVEN `the person intends to use the equipment or type of equipment for personal use and requests the Authority to test it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is radio-communication equipment that is not type-approved equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 31: the Authority may test the equipment and, in its discretion, impose the fees in the Third Schedule` MEANS
    `the person intends to use the equipment or type of equipment for personal use and requests the Authority to test it` AND (NOT `the equipment is radio-communication equipment that is not type-approved equipment`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:630 | Offence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:631 | 32. Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with any of the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:632 | provisions of these Regulations shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 32 (offence) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:630-632)
GIVEN `the person contravenes or fails to comply with a provision of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 32: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the person contravenes or fails to comply with a provision of the Regulations`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:634 | Composition of offences
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:635 | 33. An employee of the Authority specially authorised by name in
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:636 | that behalf by the Chief Executive may, in his discretion, compound
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:637 | any offence under these Regulations by collecting from the person
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:638 | reasonably suspected of committing an offence a sum not exceeding
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:639 | $1,000.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 33 (composition of offences) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:634-639)
GIVEN sum IS A NUMBER
      `the employee of the Authority is specially authorised by name by the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 33: the employee may compound the offence by collecting the sum from a person reasonably suspected of committing it` MEANS
    `the employee of the Authority is specially authorised by name by the Chief Executive` AND sum AT MOST 1000

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:641 | Waiver and exemption
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:642 | 34. The Minister or the Authority may, subject to any directions by
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:643 | the Minister, waive any or all of the terms and conditions in any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:644 | licence and fee payable under these Regulations and exempt any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:645 | person from any or all of the provisions of these Regulations.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 34 (waiver and exemption) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:641-645)
GIVEN `the Minister or the Authority acts subject to any directions by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 34: the Minister or the Authority may waive any or all terms and conditions in any licence and fee payable and exempt any person from any or all of the provisions` MEANS `the Minister or the Authority acts subject to any directions by the Minister`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:647 | FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:648 | Regulations 20 and 23
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:650 | TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT THE IMPORT,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:651 | MANUFACTURE, SALE, OFFER OR POSSESSION FOR SALE
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:652 | OF WHICH IS PROHIBITED
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:654 | 1. Scanning Receivers.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:656 | 2. Military Communication Equipment.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:658 | 3. Scramblers, Speech Invertors, On-line Cyphering Equipment.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:660 | 4. Telephone Voice Changing Equipment.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:662 | 5. Automatic Call Diverters.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:664 | 6. Cordless Telephone (CT1)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:665 | Operating in frequency bands 890−915MHz and 935−960MHz.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:667 | 7. Wireless Surveillance Video Camera
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:668 | Operating in frequency bands 890−915MHz and 935−960MHz.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:670 | 8. Radio-communication Jamming Devices operating in any frequency band.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule (equipment the import, manufacture, sale, offer or possession for sale of which is prohibited) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:647-670)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule: the equipment named` MEANS
    LIST "Scanning Receivers", "Military Communication Equipment", "Scramblers, Speech Invertors, On-line Cyphering Equipment", "Telephone Voice Changing Equipment", "Automatic Call Diverters"
       , "Cordless Telephone (CT1) operating in frequency bands 890-915MHz and 935-960MHz", "Wireless Surveillance Video Camera operating in frequency bands 890-915MHz and 935-960MHz", "Radio-communication Jamming Devices operating in any frequency band"

GIVEN item IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule: the equipment is named` MEANS elem item (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule: the equipment named`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:674 | SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:675 | Regulation 24 (5)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:677 | FEES FOR APPLICATION BY DEALERS FOR APPROVAL OF
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:678 | TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:680 | First column Second column Third column
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:681 | Modification
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:682 | Type of telecommunication equipment Application fee or re-test fee
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:683 | LINE-BASED EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:684 | 1. Call Switching System/Multiplex System $1,200 $600
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:685 | (a) ATM UNI Equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:686 | (b) PABX
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:687 | (c) Key Telephone System
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:688 | (d) Multi-Line System
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:689 | (e) Voice Messaging System
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:690 | (f) ISDN Equipment (Primary Rate)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:691 | (g) ISDN Equipment (Basic Rate with
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:692 | built-in NT-1)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:694 | 2. Complex Terminal Equipment $ 900 $450
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:695 | (a) ISDN Equipment (Basic Rate)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:696 | (b) ISDN Equipment (Standalone NT-1)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:697 | (c) Coinphone/Payphone
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:699 | 3. Single Line Terminal Equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:700 | (a) Telephone/Telephone Line interface/ $ 700 $350
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:701 | Telephone Ancillary/Autodialler/
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:702 | Auto Answering Set/Security Alarm
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:703 | System/Modem/EFTPOS/CCAT
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:704 | (b) Caller Identification Device/Fax $ 900 $450
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:705 | Transceiver/Fax Modem/Telex
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:706 | Equipment/Digital Leased Circuit
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:707 | Equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:716 | SECOND SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:718 | First column Second column Third column
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:719 | Modification
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:720 | Type of telecommunication equipment Application fee or re-test fee
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:721 | RADIO-COMMUNICATION
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:722 | EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:723 | 1. Analogue Radio-communication $2,000 $1,000
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:724 | Equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:725 | (a) VHF/UHF Mobile Transceiver
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:726 | (b) Trunked Radio Transceiver
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:727 | (c) Mobile Data Transceiver
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:728 | (d) Cordless Telephone (CT2/CT3)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:730 | 2. Analogue Cellular Mobile Phone $1,500 $ 750
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:731 | (AMPS/ETACS)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:733 | 3. Radio Pager/Two-way Pager $1,300 $ 650
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:735 | 4. Amateur Radio Transceiver $1,000 $ 500
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:737 | 5. Dual-Band Digital Cellular Mobile $ 570 $ 285
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:738 | Phone
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:740 | 6. Digital Cellular Mobile Phone $ 350 $ 175
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:741 | (GSM/DCS/CDMA)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:743 | 7. Digital Cordless Telephone $ 350 $ 175
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:744 | (DECT/PHS) (Fixed or Mobile)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:746 | 8. Wireless LAN Transceiver $ 350 $ 175
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:748 | 9. Low Power Device $ 350 $ 175
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:750 | 10. Low Power Device (where testing by $ 460 $ 230.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:751 | the Authority is required)
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Second Schedule (fees for application by dealers for approval of telecommunication equipment) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:674-751)
GIVEN item IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Second Schedule: the application fee and the modification or re-test fee in dollars (in that order)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF item EQUALS "Line-based 1 Call Switching System/Multiplex System" THEN JUST (LIST 1200, 600)
           IF item EQUALS "Line-based 2 Complex Terminal Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 900, 450)
           IF item EQUALS "Line-based 3(a) Telephone/Telephone Line interface/Telephone Ancillary/Autodialler/Auto Answering Set/Security Alarm System/Modem/EFTPOS/CCAT" THEN JUST (LIST 700, 350)
           IF item EQUALS "Line-based 3(b) Caller Identification Device/Fax Transceiver/Fax Modem/Telex Equipment/Digital Leased Circuit Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 900, 450)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 1 Analogue Radio-communication Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 2000, 1000)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 2 Analogue Cellular Mobile Phone (AMPS/ETACS)" THEN JUST (LIST 1500, 750)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 3 Radio Pager/Two-way Pager" THEN JUST (LIST 1300, 650)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 4 Amateur Radio Transceiver" THEN JUST (LIST 1000, 500)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 5 Dual-Band Digital Cellular Mobile Phone" THEN JUST (LIST 570, 285)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 6 Digital Cellular Mobile Phone (GSM/DCS/CDMA)" THEN JUST (LIST 350, 175)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 7 Digital Cordless Telephone (DECT/PHS) (Fixed or Mobile)" THEN JUST (LIST 350, 175)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 8 Wireless LAN Transceiver" THEN JUST (LIST 350, 175)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 9 Low Power Device" THEN JUST (LIST 350, 175)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 10 Low Power Device (where testing by the Authority is required)" THEN JUST (LIST 460, 230)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:755 | THIRD SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:756 | Regulation 31
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:758 | FEES FOR TESTS DONE ON EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:759 | FOR INDIVIDUAL USE
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:761 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:762 | Test fee Re-test fee
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:763 | LINE-BASED EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:764 | 1. Standard Telephone $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:765 | 2. Modem $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:766 | 3. Call Switching/Multiplex System $500 $250
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:767 | 4. Other Terminal Equipment $200 $100
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:769 | RADIO-COMMUNICATION
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:770 | EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:771 | 1. Cellular Mobile Phone $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:772 | 2. Cordless Telephone $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:773 | 3. Amateur Radio Transceiver $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:774 | 4. Low Power Device $ 55 $ 28
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:775 | 5. Wireless LAN Transceiver $ 55 $ 28
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:776 | 6. Other Radio-communication Equipment $200 $100.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Third Schedule (fees for tests done on equipment for individual use) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:755-776)
GIVEN item IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Third Schedule: the test fee and the re-test fee in dollars (in that order)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF item EQUALS "Line-based 1 Standard Telephone" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF item EQUALS "Line-based 2 Modem" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF item EQUALS "Line-based 3 Call Switching/Multiplex System" THEN JUST (LIST 500, 250)
           IF item EQUALS "Line-based 4 Other Terminal Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 200, 100)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 1 Cellular Mobile Phone" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 2 Cordless Telephone" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 3 Amateur Radio Transceiver" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 4 Low Power Device" THEN JUST (LIST 55, 28)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 5 Wireless LAN Transceiver" THEN JUST (LIST 55, 28)
           IF item EQUALS "Radio-communication 6 Other Radio-communication Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 200, 100)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:785 | FOURTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:786 | Regulation 4A
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:788 | DEALER’S CLASS LICENCE CONDITIONS
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:790 | 1. In these conditions, ‘‘relevant telecommunication equipment’’ means the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:791 | telecommunication equipment manufactured, imported, hired, sold, offered or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:792 | possessed for sale by the holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:794 | 2. A holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:795 | (a) unless he holds a Dealer’s Individual Licence, register with the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:796 | Authority in such form as the Authority may require in respect of each
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:797 | of the premises under his control or occupation at which he
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:798 | manufactures, imports, hires, sells, offers or possesses for sale any
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:799 | telecommunication equipment;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:800 | (b) submit in writing to the Authority such information as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:801 | may require relating to its particulars, and the description and scope of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:802 | its business dealings in the relevant telecommunication equipment; and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:803 | (c) inform the Authority of any change of the information submitted to the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:804 | Authority under sub-paragraph (b).
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:806 | 3. A holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall comply with the standards and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:807 | specifications published by the Authority from time to time in relation to the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:808 | relevant telecommunication equipment.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:810 | 4. A holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall, if required by the Authority,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:811 | produce at his expense any relevant telecommunication equipment for testing or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:812 | inspection by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:814 | 5. A holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall not have in his possession —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:815 | (a) any telecommunication equipment that is not type-approved equipment;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:816 | (b) any device or equipment that is capable of monitoring or intercepting the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:817 | transmissions of a radio-communication network; or
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:818 | (c) any device or equipment that can be used to insert or duplicate the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:819 | identification of an authorised telecommunication equipment to an
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:820 | unauthorised telecommunication equipment.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:822 | 6. A holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall comply with the Authority’s
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:823 | policies and directions in relation to the relevant telecommunication equipment as
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:824 | specified from time to time.
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Fourth Schedule (Dealer's Class Licence conditions) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:785-824)
GIVEN `unless he holds a Dealer's Individual Licence, the holder registered with the Authority in respect of each of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder submitted in writing the information the Authority requires on its particulars and the description and scope of its business dealings, and informed it of any change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder complies with the standards and specifications published by the Authority in relation to the relevant equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder, if required by the Authority, produced the relevant equipment at its expense for testing or inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder has in his possession telecommunication equipment that is not type-approved equipment, or a device capable of monitoring or intercepting the transmissions of a radio-communication network, or a device that can be used to insert or duplicate the identification of authorised equipment in unauthorised equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder complies with the Authority's policies and directions in relation to the relevant equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Fourth Schedule items 1 to 6: the holder of a Dealer's Class Licence is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        `unless he holds a Dealer's Individual Licence, the holder registered with the Authority in respect of each of the premises`
    AND `the holder submitted in writing the information the Authority requires on its particulars and the description and scope of its business dealings, and informed it of any change`
    AND `the holder complies with the standards and specifications published by the Authority in relation to the relevant equipment`
    AND `the holder, if required by the Authority, produced the relevant equipment at its expense for testing or inspection`
    AND (NOT `the holder has in his possession telecommunication equipment that is not type-approved equipment, or a device capable of monitoring or intercepting the transmissions of a radio-communication network, or a device that can be used to insert or duplicate the identification of authorised equipment in unauthorised equipment`)
    AND `the holder complies with the Authority's policies and directions in relation to the relevant equipment`

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:828 | FIFTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:829 | Regulations 4, 4A,
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:830 | 24 (2) and 24A
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:832 | TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:833 | NOT REQUIRING APPROVAL
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:835 | 1. Telephone (Standard/Multi-Feature/Image/Data/Switching)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:837 | 2. Telephone Line Interface
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:839 | 3. Telephone Ancillary
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:841 | 4. Autodialler
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:843 | 5. Auto Answering/Recording Set
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:845 | 6. Caller Identification Equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:847 | 7. Security Alarm System
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:849 | 8. Facsimile Transceiver
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:851 | 9. Modem
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:853 | 10. EFTPOS/CCAT
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:855 | 11. Telex Equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:857 | 12. Digital Leased Circuit Equipment
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:859 | 13. Other equipment as determined by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99:860 | [G.N. Nos. S 327/94; S 88/95; S 70/96; S 425/96; S 166/98; S 540/98]
@ref Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Fifth Schedule (telecommunication equipment not requiring approval) (src:TA1999-DEAL99:828-860)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Fifth Schedule: the equipment named` MEANS
    LIST "Telephone (Standard/Multi-Feature/Image/Data/Switching)", "Telephone Line Interface", "Telephone Ancillary", "Autodialler", "Auto Answering/Recording Set", "Caller Identification Equipment"
       , "Security Alarm System", "Facsimile Transceiver", "Modem", "EFTPOS/CCAT", "Telex Equipment", "Digital Leased Circuit Equipment", "Other equipment as determined by the Authority"

GIVEN item IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Fifth Schedule: the equipment is named` MEANS elem item (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) Fifth Schedule: the equipment named`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- S 362/2001, the Telecommunication (Dealers) (Amendment) Regulations 2001: first published 30 July 2001 at 5:00 pm, made 27 July 2001, in operation 1 August 2001 except reg 4(a), which is deemed in operation on 21 January 2000.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:15 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 74 of the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:16 | Telecommunications Act, the Info-communications Development
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:17 | Authority of Singapore, with the approval of the Minister for
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:18 | Communications and Information Technology, hereby makes the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:19 | following Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:21 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:22 | 1.—(1) These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:23 | (Dealers) (Amendment) Regulations 2001 and shall, with the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:24 | exception of regulation 4 (a), come into operation on 1st August 2001.
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:25 | (2) Regulation 4 (a) shall be deemed to have come into operation
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:26 | on 21st January 2000.
@ref Rg 7 as amended by S 362/2001: enacting words, citation and commencement (src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:15-26)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 S 362/2001 reg 1: the amendment other than reg 4(a) is in operation on the date (from 1 August 2001)` MEANS d AT LEAST (Date 1 8 2001)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 S 362/2001 reg 1(2): reg 4(a) is deemed to have come into operation on the date (from 21 January 2000)` MEANS d AT LEAST (Date 21 1 2000)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:28 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 15
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:29 | 2. Regulation 15 of the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:30 | (Rg 7) (referred to in these Regulations as the principal Regulations)
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:31 | is deleted and the following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:32 | ‘‘Inspection of Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:33 | 15. A holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall permit
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:34 | an authorised officer or a police officer not below the rank of
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:35 | sergeant, upon production of proof of identity, to inspect his
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:36 | licence or, if it is not immediately available, require its
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:37 | production within a reasonable period at the office of the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:38 | Authority or a police station named by the police officer.’’.
@ref Rg 7 reg 15 as substituted by S 362/2001 regulation 2 (src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:28-38)
GIVEN `the holder permits an authorised officer or a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, upon production of proof of identity, to inspect his licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence is not immediately available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder produces it within a reasonable period at the office of the Authority or a police station named by the police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 reg 15 as substituted by S 362/2001: the holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence is meeting the regulation` MEANS
        `the holder permits an authorised officer or a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, upon production of proof of identity, to inspect his licence`
    AND ((NOT `the licence is not immediately available`) OR `the holder produces it within a reasonable period at the office of the Authority or a police station named by the police officer`)

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:41 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 32
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:42 | 3. Regulation 32 of the principal Regulations is deleted and the
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:43 | following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:44 | ‘‘Offence
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:45 | 32. Any person who contravenes regulation 4 (1) or (4), 6 (2),
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:46 | 12 (2), 14, 15, 17, 18, 19 or 20 (3) or (4) shall be guilty of an
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:47 | offence.’’.
@ref Rg 7 reg 32 as substituted by S 362/2001 regulation 3 (src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:41-47)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 reg 32 as substituted by S 362/2001: a contravention of this regulation is an offence` MEANS
    elem provision (LIST "4(1)", "4(4)", "6(2)", "12(2)", "14", "15", "17", "18", "19", "20(3)", "20(4)")

-- Reg 32 as in the 1999 Edition: "Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with any of the provisions of these Regulations shall be guilty of an offence" (above); from 1 August 2001 only the provisions S 362/2001 names.
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
      `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 7 reg 32: a contravention of the provision is an offence, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (`conduct day` LESS THAN (Date 1 12 1999)) OR (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 2 4 2003)) OR (`reading day` LESS THAN (Date 1 7 1999)) THEN NOTHING
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 30 7 2001)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 1 8 2001)) THEN JUST (`Rg 7 reg 32 as substituted by S 362/2001: a contravention of this regulation is an offence` provision)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:49 | Amendment of First Schedule
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:50 | 4. The First Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:51 | (a) by deleting item 3;
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:52 | (b) by deleting item 6 and substituting the following item:
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:53 | ‘‘6. Radio-communication Equipment operating in frequency bands
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:54 | 890-915 MHz and 935-960 MHz except Cellular Mobile phones
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:55 | or such other equipment approved by the Authority.’’; and
-- src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:56 | (c) by deleting item 7.
@ref Rg 7 First Schedule as amended by S 362/2001 regulation 4 (src:TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001:49-56)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Rg 7 First Schedule as amended by S 362/2001 (1 August 2001): the equipment named` MEANS
    LIST "Scanning Receivers", "Military Communication Equipment", "Telephone Voice Changing Equipment", "Automatic Call Diverters"
       , "Radio-communication Equipment operating in frequency bands 890-915 MHz and 935-960 MHz except Cellular Mobile phones or such other equipment approved by the Authority"
       , "Radio-communication Jamming Devices operating in any frequency band"

-- Item 3 ("Scramblers, Speech Invertors, On-line Cyphering Equipment") is deleted by reg 4(a), deemed in operation from 21 January 2000; items 6 and 7 change from 1 August 2001.
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Rg 7 First Schedule with item 3 deleted (reg 4(a) of S 362/2001, deemed from 21 January 2000) and items 6 and 7 as in the 1999 Edition: the equipment named` MEANS
    LIST "Scanning Receivers", "Military Communication Equipment", "Telephone Voice Changing Equipment", "Automatic Call Diverters"
       , "Cordless Telephone (CT1) operating in frequency bands 890-915MHz and 935-960MHz", "Wireless Surveillance Video Camera operating in frequency bands 890-915MHz and 935-960MHz", "Radio-communication Jamming Devices operating in any frequency band"

GIVEN `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`Rg 7 First Schedule: the equipment named, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (`conduct day` LESS THAN (Date 1 12 1999)) OR (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 2 4 2003)) OR (`reading day` LESS THAN (Date 1 7 1999)) THEN NOTHING
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 30 7 2001)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 1 8 2001)) THEN JUST (`Rg 7 First Schedule as amended by S 362/2001 (1 August 2001): the equipment named`)
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 30 7 2001)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 21 1 2000)) THEN JUST (`Rg 7 First Schedule with item 3 deleted (reg 4(a) of S 362/2001, deemed from 21 January 2000) and items 6 and 7 as in the 1999 Edition: the equipment named`)
           OTHERWISE JUST (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule: the equipment named`)
